1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:07,550
Diwan-i-Khas is identified in historic records as the Hall of Private Audience of the Red Fort.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:14,212
Its construction period is recorded from AD 1639 to 1648.

3
00:00:14,212 --> 00:00:21,662
Unlike the public court, the emperor gave audience here specifically to select courtiers and nobles.

4
00:00:21,662 --> 00:00:29,112
This restricted audience made Diwan-i-Khas an exclusive center for private imperial council.

5
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:35,175
The people named in the historical record were select nobles and high courtiers.

6
00:00:35,175 --> 00:00:40,125
The presiding figure giving private audience was the Mughal emperor.

7
00:00:40,125 --> 00:00:44,675
The hall had two courtyards situated on its west side.

8
00:00:44,675 --> 00:00:50,612
Both of these western courtyards were enclosed by arcaded colonnades.

9
00:00:50,612 --> 00:00:55,937
The Nahr-i-Bihisht channel ran directly through the centre of Diwan-i-Khas.

10
00:00:55,937 --> 00:01:01,300
Diwan-i-Khas is listed as part of the protected Red Fort monument.

11
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:10,500
Its recorded history connects the date of construction between 1639 and 1648 to its imperial function.

12
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:17,137
The presence of select courtiers and nobles defined the private nature of assembly here.

13
00:01:17,137 --> 00:01:24,150
Enclosed by colonnades and courtyards, the hall offered a secluded space for governance.

14
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:29,862
The central stream of the Nahr-i-Bihisht added water to this private court setting.

15
00:01:29,862 --> 00:01:36,512
These facts document the solemn historical role of Diwan-i-Khas within the palace complex.

16
00:01:36,512 --> 00:01:42,100
The Hall of Private Audience remains a preserved component of the Red Fort.

17
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:48,200
Its identity as a private court is preserved in the official archival inventory.

18
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:53,512
Together, these recorded details form the history of Diwan-i-Khas.

